\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Polish c.bank chief cautions on zloty appreciation.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Patrick Graham   \par \uc2 559 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2005\par 18:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Feb 4 (Reuters) - Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief warned financial markets on Friday against betting on a continued climb in the zloty, saying unfinished budget reforms could bring increased volatility.   \par \par \uc2 A new wave of largely foreign buying this week pushed up the zloty and other central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reviving a debate on when its gains will hurt exports, the main driver of Poland's rapid economic recovery since 2002.   \par \par \uc2 The zloty firmed to under four per euro for the first time in over two years on Thursday, prompting the rare reaction from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Leszek Balcerowicz. "It would be risky to assume the zloty's appreciation will be a lasting trend," Balcerowicz said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2 "We know from experience that no trend lasts forever. The zloty rate has shown large volatility in the past, while structural problems of public finances, which were an important source of this volatility, did not vanish," he said.   \par \par \uc2 His comments had no impact on the zloty, but many local bond investors now believe further zloty gains could force the bank to cut interest rates faster than expected, even as early as March or April.   \par \par \uc2 Bond yields fell 20 basis points on Friday as investors brought forward bets on when the first cut would come. Previously most analysts backed a mid-year cut after an expected shift to a neutral policy bias from tightening this month.   \par \par \uc2 Last month the bank left its benchmark rate at 6.50 percent, where it has been since August 2004 after rising 125 basis points in the previous three months.   \par \par \uc2 "One option is Balcerowicz is making an excuse for not cutting rates - that he thinks the zloty will fall later this year and stop threatening to cause inflation to undershoot," said Robert Beange, economist with Lehman Brothers in London.   \par \par \uc2 "The other is he's trying to stem new capital inflows which would strengthen the zloty, make inflation undershoot and potentially lead to greater volatility later."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  UNLIKELY   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has so far kept a hands-off approach to the free-floating zloty, unlike the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in fellow EU newcomer Slovakia, which has used market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , interest rate cuts and verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.   \par \par \uc2 But over recent months the government has grown increasingly wary of the impact of the zloty's 20 percent rise against the euro since Poland's European Union entry in May.   \par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Jerzy Hausner on Thursday called on the bank to change its monetary policy line to prevent further gains which he said could hurt exporters' profitability and hence growth.   \par \par \uc2 Yet a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey on Friday showed many exporters can swallow a zloty rate of less than 4 to the euro. It also showed half are ready to use the purchasing power from the strong zloty to buy imports and spark a long-awaited investment boom this year.   \par \par \uc2 Clear prospects of lower interest rates could help ease the buying pressure on the zloty by making returns on zloty-denominated assets less attractive to foreign investors.   \par \par \uc2 Balcerowicz is due to meet government ministers on Monday to discuss Poland's plans for euro adoption, but officials have insisted the meeting is not meant to produce any immediate action to counter the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050204e12400dwu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
