\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -C.Europe rangebound, eyes euro/dlr moves.  \b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2005\par 12:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 21 (Reuters) - Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hugged narrow ranges on Friday, struggling to find upward momentum even though the euro managed to haul itself off two-month lows against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 A cautious tone prevailed across \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, with the dollar still within a cent of two-month highs against the euro , despite its softer tone.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. rate outlook is seen key to near-term moves. Federal Reserve officials continued to hint on Thursday U.S. interest rates would rise only steadily, though the prospect of higher U.S. yields has buoyed the dollar so far this year.  \par \par \uc2 The region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been tracking euro/dollar moves closely in recent weeks, but after last year's strong gains analysts said further upside might be hard won.  \par \par \uc2 "Irrespective of euro/dollar, ultimately these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  seem less attractive than they were a few months ago so we might actually see some weakness, but it also depends whether we get calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Dwyfor Evans, emerging markets analyst at Bank of America.  \par \par \uc2 "Euro/dollar still holds the key but it's not looking particularly promising for the high-yield regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given the rate and potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  backdrop," he said.  \par \par \uc2 This year has seen officials in \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Hungary express growing concern that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength is hurting the domestic economy, while the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already stepped in to curb crown strength.  \par \par \uc2 Evans also said signs of downward inflation pressure in the region could also work as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  negative, adding to the case for lower interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 ZLOTY, FORINT RANGEBOUND  \par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty traded sideways after data on Thursday showed industrial output and producer prices grew more slowly than expected in December, fuelling expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may change its interest rate policy bias soon.  \par \par \uc2 Industrial output grew at an annual pace of 6.4 percent, well below a consensus forecast of 13 percent, while producer price inflation slowed to 5.6 percent, from 6.7 percent the previous month.  \par \par \uc2 In a Reuters interview earlier this week, monetary policy council member Halina Wasilewska-Trenkner said falling inflation may allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to change its policy bias to "neutral" from "restrictive" after the first quarter.  \par \par \uc2 "The numbers were pretty weak and this increases the speculation that there will be a move to a neutral bias from restrictive bias at the monetary policy council meeting next week," said Lars Christensen, analyst at Danske Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Christensen said an early dip in the zloty had been on speculation of a more dovish stance from the MPC, though it later recovered the lost ground.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 1114 GMT, the zloty traded at 4.0856 against the euro  from late\par 4.0905 late on Thursday and at 3.1452 to the dollar        from\par 3.1663.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian forint also traded calmly, with ongoing investor concerns over the fiscal outlook still being offset by the country's attractive yields.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Opposition leader Viktor Orban said on Thursday Hungary would have to follow neighbouring countries like Slovakia and Romania in adopting flat taxes, if it wants to attract foreign investment inflows.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Orban, whose centre-right Fidesz party is just ahead in the polls ahead of a 2006 general election, also said a change of government was vital if the country were to join the euro zone by 2010.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Any move towards discussing tax reform in Hungary is a positive because that would be investor-friendly and in the longer-run a positive for the forint as long as the markets believe that it could be done without harming public finances," Christensen said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The forint traded flat at 246.71 against the euro .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050121e11l00b6v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
