\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Stronger zloty could hit growth-c.bank's Slawinski.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Tomasz Janowski and Pawel Florkiewicz  \par \uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2004\par 15:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Dec 20 (Reuters) - A strengthening zloty has further improved Poland's inflation outlook, but more fast gains could hurt growth and pose a serious challenge to monetary policy, a member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy council said on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Last week the 10-member rate-setting body held its key rate unchanged at 6.50 percent for the fourth month running, citing the strong zloty's dampening impact on inflation. "The balance of inflation risks is improving, mainly because of zloty appreciation. It is hard to see any serious threats on the demand side," Andrzej Slawinski told Reuters in an interview.  \par \par \uc2 "But the appreciation, if it continues at the same pace, can become a potential threat to growth," he said. "This would be a serious problem for monetary policy, which aims to stabilise inflation in the medium term and minimise short term swings in economic growth."  \par \par \uc2 The zloty climbed 14 percent against the euro this year, sparking a debate among policymakers as to what, if anything, could be done to prevent a further climb from hurting growth and disrupting Poland's preparations for the euro.  \par \par \uc2 Slawinski declined to say how the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which for years has maintained a hands-off policy to the free-floating zloty, should act if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's climb continued.  \par \par \uc2 ZLOTY PEG  \par \par \uc2 Slawinski said it was crucial to avoid pegging the zloty to the euro in the ERM-2 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grid at an excessively strong rate and that \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  could become more likely in the run-up to the mechanism.  \par \par \uc2 "It is very important to enter ERM-2 with an exchange rate which is not overvalued," Slawinski said, adding the desired equilibrium exchange rate was set to keep on changing to reflect structural changes in the Polish economy.  \par \par \uc2 "The approach of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's entry to ERM-2 may make \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market more likely, even though they don't need to be frequent," he said. He added sound budget policy was the best way to prevent market speculation.  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry has said Poland could already join in early 2006 and adopt the euro in 2009, but financial markets are less optimistic and Slawinski said the timing would hinge on progress in cutting future budget deficits.  \par \par \uc2 Slawinski, considered an expert on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, said fellow EU newcomer Slovakia chose to counter excessive market moves with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rate cuts, while accepting fundamental strengthening of its crown.  \par \par \uc2 "In today's globalised \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets it is very difficult for central banks to counter exchange rate trends. They can only try to slow the trend ... seeking out moments when \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be effective and not too expensive," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Many economists believe zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be doomed to fail and advocate easing of monetary policy instead to make zloty assets less attractive to foreign investors.  \par \par \uc2 Two fellow council members have said the bank could consider a shift to a neutral bias after the first quarter of 2005 if the zloty stayed strong and wages moderate, but Slawinski declined to discuss the timing of such a move.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041220e0ck00fda\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
