\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Polish zloty to gain below 4.0 vs euro-Orlowski.   \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2004\par 10:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Dec 9 (Reuters) - The zloty could strengthen past 4.0 to the euro within half a year, the President's chief economic aide said on Thursday, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the Polish unit would make no sense now.   \par \par \uc2 The zloty has enjoyed a steady climb against a globally strong euro in the past nine months but a 20-month high against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit last week revived talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "The zloty will be strong ... it will break the psychological level of 4.0 versus the euro and some 3.0 zlotys to the dollar within half a year," Witold Orlowski told private radio PIN."But I can also imagine a scenario of the zloty's stabilisation at the level of 4.1-4.2 versus the euro."   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen 14 percent against the euro and 26 percent against a falling dollar since Poland's entry to the European Union in May. Thursday mid-morning, it was trading at 4.17 against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and 3.13 versus the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Last week both the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Krzysztof Rybinski and Prime Minister Marek Belka sounded concern over what Belka called the zloty's "worrying, very fast appreciation" which could hurt \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-driven economy.   \par \par \uc2 Rybinski reminded the market that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one tool which the bank can use to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But Orlowski added his voice to signals made by the bank's governor Leszek Balcerowicz that there was no need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  make sense when the market has an idea of what will happen to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and when it is not based on solid fundamentals. Then it is enough to spook the market a little," Orlowski said.   \par \par \uc2 "Now ... the market strongly believes that the zloty is strong and will remain strong and has reasons for this. In such a situation one should ask whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not like trying to hold back the waves."    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041209e0c9005hi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
