\par\par \b \uc2 Polish MinFin sees no need for  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 135 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2004\par 13:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Dec 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry sees no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the wake of recent zlotys strengthening, a finance minister's adviser said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 "The finance ministry sees no need to interfere in the free-floating zloty exchange rate," Przemyslaw Kwiecien told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's survey showed companies pointed to 4.1 zlotys to the euro as a minimum level of profitability, so... excessive zloty strengthening could have a negative impact on corporate earnings and economic growth," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "But the free-floating rate exchange regime works well."   \par \par \uc2 Earlier on Thursday, Prime Minister Marek Belka said he wanted to meet with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to discuss exchange rate policy in light of the zloty's recent appreciation.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041202e0c2007i9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
