\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Polish PM wants c.bank meeting over zloty climb.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Wojciech Moskwa and Ewa Krukowska   \par \uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2004\par 18:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Dec 2 (Reuters) - Poland's government on Thursday called for prompt talks with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  about the zloty's surge, concerned a further climb could complicate the EU newcomer's planned euro adoption later this decade.   \par \par \uc2 But the finance ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said they saw no need for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now, as the zloty hovered near 20-month highs against the globally strong euro.   \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Marek Belka's call for a meeting follows a series of conflicting signals from policymakers about the economic impact of the strong zloty, which has gained 19 percent against the euro since hitting 2004 lows nine months ago.   \par \par \uc2 "We don't have time to wait because what is happening on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is potentially quite worrisome," Belka told reporters in Katowice, adding that a meeting with top central bankers should take place within two weeks.   \par \par \uc2 European Minister Jaroslaw Pietras said the initiative came after a recent cabinet discussion about Poland's European strategy raised concerns the zloty uptrend could have a major impact on growth and euro adoption plans.   \par \par \uc2 If Poland is to join the pre-euro ERM-2 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grid in early 2006, as the government wants, Warsaw and EU partners will soon have to begin discussions over exchange rate at which the zloty will lock into the euro.   \par \par \uc2 "We need to start thinking right now about the exchange rate at which we will join the euro zone," Pietras told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 Anchoring the zloty to the euro at too strong a rate could hurt \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's competitiveness for decades, say analysts.   \par \par \uc2 NO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  FOR NOW   \par \par \uc2 The zloty eased nearly half a percent to 4.166 against the euro.   \par \par \uc2 A day after his deputy reminded financial markets that \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were in a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's toolbox, Governor Leszek Balcerowicz played down the chances of any near-term action, adding that the economy was coping well with zloty strength.   \par \par \uc2 "We are among the countries that conduct a direct inflation target policy, with a floating zloty exchange rate set by markets. This strategy has been and is serving Poland well," Balcerowicz told public radio.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the government-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting would likely concentrate on what, if anything, Poland could do to limit zloty appreciation in the future, not on potential \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a change of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime now.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will most likely not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the next several months, when the exchange rate is still acceptable," said Stanislaw Gomulka, chief economist at Polish insurer PZU and a former Balcerowicz adviser.   \par \par \uc2 "But the question is what will happen when we will go below 4 zlotys to the euro and I think Belka wants to open a debate on what to do then," he added.   \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry said excessive zloty gains would hurt corporate earnings and growth, pointing to a rate of 4.1 zlotys per euro as a pain threshold firms could still live with.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the meeting proposal but Jan Czekaj, a member of the bank's rate setting council, said "if the prime minister invites us, we will surely meet".   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said what they heard from policymakers amounted to a cacophony of voices that could not even be treated as a "verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".   \par \par \uc2 "Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually precedes the actual one ... What is happening now is rather seen as talk that will not translate into actions," said Bank BPH analyst Marcin Mrowiec.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041202e0c2006ki\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
