\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2  revives  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2  talk as euro nears.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Wojciech Moskwa  \par \uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2004\par 16:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Nov 30 (Reuters) - "\b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " reappeared in the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vocabulary on Tuesday, revealing growing concern about the strengthening zloty as the day it is pegged to the euro draws closer, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 After years of hands-off policy and rhetoric towards the free-floating zloty, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it can always use \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to counter unwanted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings, stunning analysts but leaving the buoyant zloty unfazed.  \par \par \uc2 In unusually candid comments, deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Krzysztof Rybinski also told a news conference that the zloty's recent strength did not fully reflect economic reality and that speculative flows which boosted it to recent highs may reverse.  \par \par \uc2 Since Poland joined the European Union in May, the zloty has gained nearly 14 percent versus the globally strong euro on the back of solid economic growth, progress on fiscal reforms and a respite in political uncertainty.  \par \par \uc2 In a closed-door meeting with commercial bank economists later on Tuesday, Rybinski spelled out the reasons behind his comments, according to analysts who attended the meeting.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is worried about further zloty appreciation. Rybinski said the change in its rhetoric may be linked to Poland's nearing ERM-2 entry," said one analyst, speaking of the mandatory pre-euro Exchange Rate Mechanism \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime.  \par \par \uc2 The government has said that Poland could join ERM-2, a managed floating band around a set parity level versus the euro, as early as in the first half of 2006. If the zloty locks into the euro at too strong a level, Poland's exports would suffer.  \par \par \uc2 An overvalued zloty could also spell trouble if market concerns emerged about the credibility of Warsaw's economic policies, forcing repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Setting the parity rate involves negotiations between \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the EU executive Commission and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as well as a market reference period.  \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said there was no single path to the euro, which all new EU members want to adopt by 2010.  \par \par \uc2 Poland's hands-off approach contrasts with that in Hungary or Slovakia where central bankers have repeatedly dipped in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets or used interest rates to steer exchange rates.  \par \par \uc2 CLOSER SCRUTINY  \par \par \uc2 Another analyst who met with Rybinski said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not say what it believes should be the zloty's parity, but said the subject must be more closely scrutinised by markets.  \par \par \uc2 "If the results of this analysis are different than the situation on the market, then perhaps actions can be taken," said the analyst, referring to Rybinski's statement.  \par \par \uc2 Rybinski's comments were made during the presentation of the bank's quarterly inflation projection, which envisages a loweer zloty than levels hit in October.  \par \par \uc2 The bank said the zloty, trading around 4.21 to the euro on Tuesday, was close to the 4.15 level cited by firms in its regular business survey as a key threshold beyond which a further gains would make exports unprofitable.  \par \par \uc2 Although Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has only one target - an inflation goal - analysts say 4.15 zlotys per euro can be judged as a good indication of what it believes to be the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fair value against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 "In our view fair value is around 4.25, so today's levels are slightly overvalued, but we are close to equilibrium," said Arkadiusz Krzesniak, economist at Deutsche Bank in Warsaw.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041130e0bu0096m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
