\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Polish c.bank signals  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2  back in play.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Tomasz Janowski  \par \uc2 616 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2004\par 19:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Nov 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signalled on Tuesday that the era of its hands-off approach to the zloty may be drawing to an end as the day it pegs its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the euro nears.  \par \par \uc2 The bank, which for years has left it to the market to set the value of the free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , warned that zloty strength no longer reflected the economy's health and revived the mantra that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were part of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's toolkit.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  hopes to adopt the euro in 2009 and this means it would need to fix the zloty to the euro in the ERM-2 managed floating band around a set parity as soon as early in 2006.  \par \par \uc2 Deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Krzysztof Rybinski said the ERM-2 was close enough for the bank to start thinking about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  both inside the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grid and in the run-up to its membership.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," he told private Radio PIN. "What if there will be too much appreciation of the exchange rate before ERM-2 entry and the country will adopt as its central parity a ... rate that will hurt its competitiveness."  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the prospect of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling the zloty in the market still looked distant, but the comments amounted to a first serious verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and revealed growing unease with the zloty's relentless climb.  \par \par \uc2 Speaking about the bank's quarterly inflation projection, Rybinski said it assumed a slightly weaker zloty would better reflect economic reality and warned speculative flows driving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to record highs could be reversed.  \par \par \uc2 "The present zloty exchange rate is overvalued based on what our models say about fundamental factors," Rybinski told a news conference.  \par \par \uc2 "This is in part a result of speculation, we are witnessing inflows of hot capital and there is a growing likelihood this trend can be reversed," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Since Poland joined the European Union in May, the zloty has gained nearly 14 percent versus the globally strong euro, buoyed by solid economic growth, progress on fiscal reforms and a respite in political uncertainty.  \par \par \uc2 TRADING PLACES  \par \par \uc2 So far government officials have occasionally expressed their concern the zloty's climb could hurt Poland's vital exports, while central bankers used to play down its negative effects and welcome its help in dampening inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Now, they swapped roles.  \par \par \uc2 The bank said the zloty was close to a 4.15 per euro level cited in its business survey as a key pain threshold for exporters, while government officials played down the strong zloty as simply a sign of the economy's success.  \par \par \uc2 "The current zloty rate is not hurting the economy. The zloty is strong because of its fundamentals," Finance Minister Miroslaw Gronicki said after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tested 18-month highs at 4.18 to the euro, unfazed by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk.  \par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Jerzy Hausner on Tuesday reiterated he did not expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a sentiment shared by analysts.  \par \par \uc2 "I think we are still quite a way from levels where we could see any action from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Oliver Weeks, an economist at Morgan Stanley in London.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said Tuesday's comments were, however, a sign that the bank was concerned market players saw the zloty as a one-way bet, lifting the risk of a sharp correction.  \par \par \uc2 "It's a warning that the zloty appreciation is causing a bubble that might burst because 'hot capital' could leave any time," said Katarzyna Zajdel-Kurowska, economist with Citibank Handlowy in Warsaw.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041130e0bu00797\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
