\par\par \b \uc2 Poland finmin - many factors at play in ERM parity.  \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2003\par 17:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Dec 18 (Reuters) - Poland's Finance Minister Andrzej Raczko said on Thursday joining the pre-euro ERM-2 system with an exchange rate near the market rate was a less risky option, but factors other than stability should be considered. The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in its preliminary guidlines for euro accession candidates such as Poland that it favoured anchoring domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the euro at a level near the market rate upon entering the Exchange Rate Mechanism regime.  \par \par \uc2 "The closer this (ERM-2 parity) rate is to the market rate, the better from the point of view of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Raczko told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 "But one always has to keep in mind that there are other factors to consider (when setting the partiy rate)," he added, though he did not name any other factors.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts believe Poland may want to join the two-year managed float regime of ERM-2 with a weaker exchange rate to boost its competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 But the Polish zloty's time in the confines of a plus/minus 15 percent trading band could be risky if speculators seek to knock it out of the range or test the resolve of the ECB to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  on track for the euro.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031218dzci003qa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
