\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Budget reform key for long-term Polish growth-c.bank.  \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2003\par 16:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LODZ, Poland, Dec 9 (Reuters) - Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Leszek Balcerowicz warned on Tuesday that only fiscal tightening will ensure long-term economic growth, saying the government's 2004 forecast of five percent was optimistic, but possible.  \par \par \uc2 Balcerowicz, an outspoken critic of fiscal loosening, said the government was running out of time to adopt much needed reforms aimed at averting the risk of a public debt blowout at the approach of European Union entry next May.  \par \par \uc2 He also sounded a calming note to markets by saying finance ministry plans to convert 250 million euros of a loan from the European Investment Bank into zlotys on the interbank market was not perceived by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as any type of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Time is working against us. The faster the cabinet reforms public finances, the more sustainable growth will be," Balcerowicz told a news conference in Lodz.  \par \par \uc2 "Five percent economic growth next year is within expectations, but this is an optimistic forecast."  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this month the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimated in its quarterly report that gross domestic product rose 3.7 percent year-on-year in the third quarter and looked poised to accelerate next year and maintain momentum in 2005.  \par \par \uc2 Commenting on last week's announcement by the finance ministry that it would go to the markets rather than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to exchange half its 500 million euro EIB loan, Balcerowicz said: "I believe in the rationale given by the ministry."  \par \par \uc2 The ministry said the transaction, stemming from the need to exchange part of the euro loan into zlotys before the end of the year, was a client-driven market transaction and was not meant in any way as a market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's zloty has been in free-float since early 2000 and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept a firm hands-off approach towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Finance Minister Andrzej Raczko has also often spoken in favour of free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime for the zloty.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031209dzc9002ro\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
