\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Ctrl Bk -3: Euro Adoption Hinges On Fiscal Stance \b0\par\par\uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2003\par 17:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  As part of its strategic shift from inflation reduction to price stability, the RPP said it was abandoning its practice of setting year-end and medium-term inflation targets. \par \par \uc2  Instead, the bank said, it will adopt a continuous CPI target similar to that used by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is applied month by month and indefinitely. \par \par \uc2  The RPP said this extended time horizon will give policymakers credibility and allow a more flexible response to short-term external shocks. \par \par \uc2  The RPP reaffirmed its commitment to bring Poland into the euro zone in 2007. \par \par \uc2  It said Poland already met four of the five conditions set in the Maastricht Treaty for candidates to adopt the euro - inflation, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability, long-term interest rates and public debt. \par \par \uc2  But the RPP said the public sector deficit remained above 5.0% of gross domestic product in 2002, well above the Maastricht ceiling of 3.0%. \par \par \uc2  According to the revised RPP strategy, cuts in public spending and faster privatization of state-owned enterprises will largely determine the scope for monetary easing in coming years. \par \par \uc2  "The moment of entry into the euro zone - and appropriate adjustments of monetary policy - will depend on the fulfillment of (Maastricht) fiscal criteria," the RPP said. \par \par \uc2  It said retention of lax fiscal policies once the zloty enters the +/-15% trading band set by the ERM II exchange rate mechanism will increase the risk of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  As a result, the panel recommended retaining the zloty's current free float until the moment of entry into ERM II and the adoption of the widest possible trading band after entry. \par \par \uc2  Any change in Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, including ERM II entry, requires joint approval by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government. A mixed team of finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials is currently negotiating details of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy beyond 2004 when Poland is to join the European Union. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Grzegorz Kolodko and senior ministry officials have repeatedly stressed the need to weaken the zloty in order to boost exports and economic growth. \par \par \uc2  They argue this could be accomplished in the short term via direct \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. In addition, Kolodko has suggested \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  might introduce a trading band before entering ERM II or devalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by adopting a below-market central parity rate upon entry. \par \par \uc2  In Wednesday's strategy document, the RPP said such a devaluation would contradict the Maastricht requirement to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability for at least two years without "excessive market volatility." \par \par \uc2  Despite its five-year time horizon, the strategy document's validity expires with the current RPP's term in January 2004. \par \par \uc2  Of the panel's 10 members, analysts expect only \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Leszek Balcerowicz - who holds his seat ex officio - to remain on a reconstituted RPP. \par \par \uc2  Poland's left-dominated parliament, which will nominate six of nine new RPP members, is expected to pack the panel with proponents of more dovish policies. \par \par \uc2  National Bank of Poland Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.nbp.pl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.nbp.pl}}}\par \par \uc2  -By David McQuaid, Dow Jones Newswires; +4822 622 2766; david.mcquaid@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030226dz2q0015o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
