\par\par \b \uc2  Poland to buy  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  to service debt-MinFin. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Justyna Pawlak \par \uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2003\par 16:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 24 (Reuters) - Poland will buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market later in this quarter of 2003 to service foreign debt, but has not done so yet despite talk that it stood behind a recent drop in the zloty, a senior official said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Deputy finance minister Ryszard Michalski moved to cool speculation that the ministry sold the zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2   earlier this week, when the unit unexpectedly plunged more than two percent in a day. \par \par \uc2  Government officials have long suggested the finance ministry would buy \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cover foreign debt servicing costs on the open market in a bid to curb the zloty's strength which they believe is damaging economic competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Michalski also reiterated the finance ministry's long-standing support for some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's full-float \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says rules out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We will be buying hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for servicing debt interest costs on market in the first quarter," Michalski told Reuters on the sidelines of a roadshow held by Poland in London to promote its upcoming euro-denominated bond issue. \par \par \uc2  "But we have not done this yet, because we are not ready. We are still preparing the infrastructure and we will be ready soon, sooner than people expect," he said. \par \par \uc2  Poland will have to repay roughly $1 billion worth of foreign debt interest this year. \par \par \uc2  The zloty  has retraced some of the lost ground by Friday, but was still trading just above its lowest level on the euro since June 2000. At 1510 GMT it traded at 4.1851 versus the euro, up from the lows at 4.2482 hit on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  FINANCE MINISTRY \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains extremely volatile because dealers are anxious about any signs of finance ministry involvement, especially after Poland's regional peer Hungary moved to curb its flyaway \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian forint's appreciation limit came under fierce attack last week, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against it on the market, cut interest rates aggressively and place restrictions on short-term deposits. \par \par \uc2  Michalski said Hungary's recent experience only underlined the need to contain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength which is plaguing eastern European countries on the verge of accession to the European Union and their subsequent adoption of the euro. \par \par \uc2  The prospects of euro zone entry are luring investors who hope to capitalise on gains in the bond market after eastern European yields converge with the lower euro levels. \par \par \uc2  Despite government pressure, the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which under Polish law has to agree to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has so far strongly rejected selling zlotys. \par \par \uc2  "We fully agree that the market should decide, but we are thinking about a civilised market," Michalski told investors during the roadshow. "It seems that the process of appreciation goes too far," he said. \par \par \uc2  "A sort of a regulated market could be a much nicer solution than the volatile, impulsive market we have...Last week's experience was very destructive and shows the market should be regulated and under control," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030124dz1o00vuh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
