\par\par \b \uc2  Polish zloty opens firmer, seen inching up. \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2003\par 09:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Jan 24 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty opened higher on Friday, recovering from a 31-month low versus the euro hit on the previous session, and dealers said the unit could post more gains thanks to improved sentiment in the region. \par \par \uc2  The debt market, hit by weak demand on a primary bond tender earlier this week and turmoil on the Hungarian market, has also strengthened, with investors returning to buy Poland's treasuries. \par \par \uc2  "We had some panic and speculative games, but it should fade away. The market might still be a bit nervous, but the zloty might firm in line with the Hungarian forint and the Czech crown," said Wojciech Trzepizur, dealer at BRE Bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  The zloty lost nearly six percent since last week's hefty rate cuts by the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors who suffered losses in the central European country moved to cut their exposure in \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Hard-hitting verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Finance Minister Grzegorz Kolodko, who said he expected EU candidate Poland to join the euro zone at a zloty/euro rate of 4.35 also helped spook the market. \par \par \uc2  "The bond market is bottoming out. Investors treated the recent fall as an opportunity to buy treasuries, which offer the highest real interest rates in the region," said Krzysztof Izdebski, dealer at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  Polish five-year treasuries yielded 5.59 percent, compared to Hungary's 6.81 percent at Thursday's fixing. Polish inflation is just 0.8 percent while Hungary's is 4.8 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also said expectations of a rate cut next week could also slightly support the unit, but stressed a 25-basis-point reduction was fully priced in. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0815 GMT - Zloty/dollar  3.8800 vs 3.9050 at 1800\par GMT on Thursday Zloty/euro           4.1834 vs 4.1983 2-yr bond yield\par (OK1204)             5.50/5.47 vs 5.56 pct 5-yr bond yield (PS0608)\par         5.58/5.56 vs 5.60 pct -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RELATED NEWS (double click to access)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   Polish Market Debt                 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   Emerging Market Debt               Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   All Emerging Markets news          CEE indicators\par   All Eastern Europe News\par   TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets\par   TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch\par   Polish macroeconomic indicators\par   Czech macroeconomic indicators\par   Slovak macroeconomic indicators\par   Hungarian macroeconomic indicators\par   Main page of Reuters banking poll -- Poland\par   LIVE PRICES & DATA\par   Polish bonds\par   Central, East European Bonds\par   Emerging Markets Bonds overview\par  -----------------------------------------------------------------  HOW TO FIND INFORMATION YOU NEED\par    :          :        :              :\par    :          :        :              :               :\par  -----------------------------------------------------------------.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030124dz1o00hae\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
