\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW-Zloty appreciation not needed to cap CPI - Rosati. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Olga Markiewicz \par \uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2002\par 15:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Nov 21 (Reuters) - Polish rate-setter Dariusz Rosati told Reuters on Thursday that further zloty appreciation would be harmful for the economy and was no longer necessary to reduce inflation. \par \par \uc2  But Rosati, one of 10 Monetary Policy Council (MPC) members, said the zloty's strength was not worrying enough to warrant \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as was the case in other east European states, or changes to Poland's free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime. \par \par \uc2  His comments signal that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has played down the role of zloty movements in its interest rate decisions, may be shifting its policy focus, which would allow for further easing in order to ease upward pressure on the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Over the last several months inflation is at a satisfactory level, where we don't want to lower it but stabilise it," Rosati, a known dove on the Council, said in an interview. \par \par \uc2  "This means that we can change the accents in monetary policy. Strengthening of the zloty exchange rate to lower inflation is no longer needed, and it is harmful." Inflation hit a post-communist low of 1.1 percent year-on-year in October and is expected miss the MPC's end-2002 2-4 percent target on the downside. \par \par \uc2  After the last rate cut in October, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said that rates were at or very near their adequate level, limiting scope for more easing after a nearly two-year cycle of cautious, gradual reductions. \par \par \uc2  Rosati said the MPC had been willing to "apply a certain dose of zloty appreciation" to limit inflation - through lowering the price of imports - but that in the present price environment the Council did not have to pay that cost. \par \par \uc2  LOWER RATES A POSSIBILITY \par \par \uc2  The zloty has gained six percent against the dollar and three versus the revved up euro over the last month, as fears surrounding Poland's 2004 accession to the European Union eased and foreign portfolio investors increasingly bet on Polish asset prices quickly converging with those in the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  Such upward pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has forced Hungary and Slovakia to cut rates in past weeks despite a far-more uncertain inflation environment than \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's. Slovakia and the Czech Republic have also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There are several possibilities. Lowering interest rates will weaken demand for zlotys stemming from rate cut expectations. We still have this possibility," Rosati said. \par \par \uc2  "Another option is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is theoretically possible but we have long indicated that such a solution would be costly and ineffective." \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a change in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime only if "we are certain that capital inflows are so large, that the zloty would appreciate to such a level that it would have to come crashing down." \par \par \uc2  "But we are still not in such a situation." \par \par \uc2  The government believes the zloty is too strong for exporters and could make Poland's economy uncompetitive if the country joins the euro-zone, expected in 2007 or 2008, before previously weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Economy Minister Jacek Piechota earlier called for a rate cut when the MPC meets on November 26-27. \par \par \uc2  "The overly strong zloty is reducing the profitability of our exporters and we are counting on cooperation from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in that respect," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021121dybl00sjx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
