\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Ctrl Bk, Govt Set Up Task Force On  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Strategy \b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2002\par 15:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW -(Dow Jones)- The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance ministry said Wednesday they have set up a task force to work out strategy for Poland's economic convergence with the euro zone, providing further evidence that an ugly policy feud between the two sides may be subsiding after mediation by President Aleksander Kwasniewski. \par \par \uc2  Deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Andrzej Bratkowski and Deputy Finance Minister Andrzej Raczko will co-chair the group, which was established by Finance Minister Marek Belka and Central Bbank President Leszek Balcerowicz. \par \par \uc2  The move comes less than a day after a two-hour meeting between Kwasniewski and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate-setting Monetary Policy Council, or RPP, which has been resisting government pressure to relax interest-rate and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies in order to boost sagging economic growth. \par \par \uc2  After that meeting, Balcerowicz said the RPP was ready to open talks with the government on ways to curb the appreciating Polish zloty and manage \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy during the run-up to Poland's entry to the European Union and the euro zone, expected in 2004 and 2007, respectively. \par \par \uc2  However, Balcerowicz said the bank did not believe it made sense to drop Poland's present \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, which since April 2000 has been based on a free-floating zloty. \par \par \uc2  Belka has been pressing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to consider adjusting exchange-rate policy since mid-May, when the government submitted confidential proposals to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . No details have been released, but Belka has publicly advocated reintroducing a trading band - perhaps similar to the ERM2 exchange rate mechanism Poland must adopt two years before entering the European Economic and Monetary Union. \par \par \uc2  Poland's parliament is now considering several bills sponsored by ruling coalition parties that would water down the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's autonomy and pack the policy-making RPP with new members. Belka and, to a lesser extent, the government, have distanced themselves from the legislation, but say it will probably pass unless the RPP eases its tough anti-inflation stance. \par \par \uc2  Tensions increased this week after the release of May consumer price data showing that annual inflation had dropped to a record-low 1.9%, from 3.0% in March. The pro-government OPZZ trade union federation said it would demonstrate at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  headquarters in Warsaw next week to protest the RPP's policies, which it claimed are responsible for high unemployment. \par \par \uc2  Late Tuesday, Finance Minister Belka said he welcomed the prospect of direct talks with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an opportunity to cool the overheated atmosphere. \par \par \uc2  Markets also appeared reassured, with the Polish zloty slightly stronger against the dollar, at PLZ4.0135 from PLZ4.0285 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Investors are now focusing on the RPP's next policy meeting June 25-26, with most participants expecting a 50- basis-point rate cut in the wake of the May price data. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said such a move could be part of a tacit understanding to defuse tensions between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government, and would mark the first time the RPP has eased rates in three consecutive months. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark 28-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is now set at 9.0%. \par \par \uc2  -By David McQuaid, Dow Jones Newswires; +4822 622 2766; david.mcquaid@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020619dy6j000u1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
