\par\par \b \uc2  Polish cabinet meets to tackle zloty strength. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Justyna Pawlak \par \uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2002\par 12:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, May 14 (Reuters) - Poland's leftist government was expected to issue a strongly-worded statement expressing its concern over the strong zloty on Tuesday and may even propose replacing its free float with a trading band, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  A bout of selling ahead of the government decision has pulled the rug from underneath the buoyant zloty - which hit four month highs versus the dollar last week - and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to lose ground in early trading. \par \par \uc2  The government's meeting started at 1000 GMT, but no time has been set for a news briefing. \par \par \uc2  Senior cabinet ministers have launched a chorus of demands on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the zloty, worried that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength is pricing Poland's already falling exports out of key western European markets. \par \par \uc2  But some analysts believe the government may go a step further, proposing to enclose the zloty in a trading band that would require the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it gets too strong. \par \par \uc2  Under Polish law such policy changes would require the approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has rejected government pleas for zloty-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But analysts now warn the government could even seek legislative amendments to the National Bank of Poland (NBP) charter in order to ensure its plans succeed. \par \par \uc2  "The government's goal has always been to depress the zloty. So now they will propose some kind of a trading band," said Krzysztof Rybinski, chief economist at bank BZ WBK in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  "But when the NBP refuses to back this, the government will seek legislative amendments to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  charter." \par \par \uc2  Other analysts said, however, they did not expect Premier Leszek Miller's cabinet to make any concrete policy proposals. Ministers blame the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's caution in gradually easing its official rates for drawing capital to Poland, which hurts exporters with high hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices for their goods. \par \par \uc2  Poland fully floated the zloty two years ago but will have to corral the unit into a 30-percentage point band when it joins the European Union's exchange rate mechanism (ERM II) after becoming the bloc's member. \par \par \uc2  Hungary, which along with Poland and the Czech Republic is a top candidate for EU entry in 2004, established an ERM-style trading band last year, while the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the fully floated Czech crown. \par \par \uc2  FUELING UNCERTAINTY \par \par \uc2  Some analysts say the government may be only bluffing to sow uncertainty in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the zloty, pointing out that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the late 1990s proved ineffectual and costly. \par \par \uc2  The recent flurry of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by senior government officials, who said the zloty should be between six and 15 percent weaker, as well as rising concern over possible legislative action have already shaken the unit. \par \par \uc2  The zloty lost 1.5 percent to the dollar and the euro in Tuesday morning trade, before rising slightly. At 0912 GMT it was still four percent down to the dollar from four-month highs it hit last week. The zloty also traded at 3.7189 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  "The market has lost its balance. Investors have become scared," said Maciej Krzak, economist at Citibank's Bank Handlowy. "The government will try to verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again but market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to be done quietly." \par \par \uc2  Central bankers argue the zloty's strength is unavoidable because the government's hefty treasury issuance and falling investment risk linked to prospects for \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's EU entry, will attract capital regardless of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the neighbouring Czech Republic, a concerted government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  effort to depress the buoyant crown failed to make significant impact earlier this year. \par \par \uc2  For a factbox on Poland's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime click here:. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020514dy5e00kj4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
