\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 3-Polish leftists to seek  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  policy changes. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Justyna Pawlak \par \uc2 703 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 2002\par 21:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Recasts with finance minister Belka comment, previous KATOWICE) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW, May 13 (Reuters) - Poland's leftist government will debate ways to depress the buoyant zloty at its Tuesday cabinet meeting with ministers hoping to convince the independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Senior cabinet ministers have already raised a chorus of demands on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the zloty in recent weeks, worried that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength is making Poland's already falling exports too pricey for European buyers. \par \par \uc2  But Finance Minister Marek Belka signalled in a late-Monday television interview that the cabinet may go a step further, proposing changes to \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime which would necessitate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty. \par \par \uc2  Such plans, however, may fall on deaf ears at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which favours the present, fully-floated zloty regime. Under Polish law, the government sets \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in agreement with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The initiative belongs to the government. We will not discuss a "specific" exchange rate to the dollar or the euro," Belka told private TVN television. "But we will discuss the direction in which (exchange rate) policy should be changed. \par \par \uc2  "This direction may be towards some form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...A trading range could be set, a soft or a hard one, disclosed or secret," he said. \par \par \uc2  Poland fully floated the zloty two years ago but it will have to close the unit in a 30-percentage point band when it joins the European Union's exchange rate mechanism (ERM II) after becoming the bloc's member. \par \par \uc2  Hungary, which along with Poland and the Czech Republic is a top candidate for EU entry in 2004, established an ERM-style trading band last year, while the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the fully floated Czech crown. \par \par \uc2  BLAMING ZLOTY \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Monday Polish Premier Leszek Miller renewed calls for a weaker zloty, which he says is needed to lift Poland from a deep growth slowdown, saying the unit's strength would be debated at Tuesday's cabinet meeting. \par \par \uc2  Ministers blame the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's caution in gradually easing its official rates for drawing capital to Poland, which hurts exporters with high hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices for their goods. \par \par \uc2  "I agree with Finance Minister Marek Belka the zloty should be at 4.25-4.30 (to the dollar). It is too strong and monetary policy is not good for the economy," Miller told a news conference in the southern city of Katowice. \par \par \uc2  The zloty, which was at four-month highs of 3.95 to the dollar last week, fell in response to ministers' verbal pressure, shedding one percent to the greenback on Monday. It was at 4.0550 to the dollar and at 3.6946 to the euro late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Late last week, Belka said he was seeking help from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bring the buoyant zloty down around 6 percent to 4.25 versus the dollar. Presidential aide Witold Orlowski went even further, calling for a 10-15 percent weakening. \par \par \uc2  After April's 50 basis point rate cut, Poland's main rate stands at 9.5 percent, 6 percentage points above CPI. \par \par \uc2  UNBENDING \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  But a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official quickly dashed cabinet hopes for imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying such a move against the zloty was "not acceptable now." Other top central bankers have said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was too costly and likely inefficient. \par \par \uc2  Bankers argue the zloty's strength is unavoidable because the government's hefty treasury issuance and falling investment risk linked to prospects for \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's EU entry, will attract capital in spite of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In neighbouring Czech Republic, a concerted government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  effort to depress the buoyant crown failed to make significant impact earlier this year. \par \par \uc2  "At this point, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not acceptable," Monetary Policy Council member Boguslaw Grabowski told Reuters in a brief interview. "You do not stand in front of a charging train." \par \par \uc2  He also repeated his support for Poland's present \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, which bankers argue gives them best means to fight inflation. "I am absolutely in favour of the present regime. If we had any doubts, we would have already proposed changes." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020513dy5d00jgi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
