\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Polish FinMin seeks talks with c.bank over zloty. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Justyna Pawlak \par \uc2 457 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2002\par 17:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  GDANSK, Poland, May 10 (Reuters) - Polish Finance Minister Marek Belka said on Friday that he was seeking talks with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at weakening the buoyant zloty by around six percent. \par \par \uc2  Belka is at loggerheads with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over what he considers an over tight monetary policy and an overvalued zloty. He said a decline in the zloty to roughly to 4.25 to the dollar would be "safe" and would aid exporters. \par \par \uc2  The zloty has hit four-month highs against the dollar this week at 3.95 and late on Friday it traded at 4.013. Versus the euro it was at 3.663, showing little impact to Belka's comments. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Minister signalled that he was interested in discussions with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over limiting the zloty's strength within the present \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime - a fully free float since April 2000 - as well as possible alternative \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimes. \par \par \uc2  "Monetary policy is a very strong factor which impacts the zloty, because it determines short-term cash flows," Belka told reporters on the sidelines of a conference between Baltic and Nordic finance ministers in the port of Gdansk. \par \par \uc2  "If on this issue (interest rates), the MPC does not see any room for manoeuvre, there exists a possibillity of a return to the broader question of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimes, or (conducting) exchange rate policy within the framework of the current regime." \par \par \uc2  Earlier this week, top government officials have called on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but bankers have said that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be fruitless. \par \par \uc2  According to \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's constitution, the government sets the country's exchange rate regime in agreement with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on the other hand, conducts day-to-day activities, such as \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Belka conceded that without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support the government could not move to change the exchange rate regime. "Without such talks with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , this is not a possibility." \par \par \uc2  This week Belka signalled that he was leaning towards a managed float \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system, saying that he was not against the reversal of a full flotation but against a fixed rate. \par \par \uc2  Poland, in line to join the European Union in 2004, will have to change its exchange rate regime before it enters the euro-zone's waiting room - the Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM-2). \par \par \uc2  Belka has said that before the ERM-2 system pegs the zloty to the euro in a 30 percent-wide trading range he would favour devaluing the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  But Poland's "hands-off" \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said that only market forces can set the zloty's value. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020510dy5a00upw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal6