\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 4-Polish gov't,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  joust over strong zloty. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Justyna Pawlak \par \uc2 744 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2002\par 20:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, May 8 (Reuters) - Senior Polish ministers, opening a new front in their battle with interest rate hawks at the independent National Bank, on Wednesday called for action to push down the buoyant zloty. \par \par \uc2  But a top central banker insisted that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets would not work. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Marek Belka called the strong zloty a "curse" on the economy and was backed by Prime Minister Leszek Miller, who demanded a big interest rate cut and called for a "more realistic level" for the zloty to help exporters. \par \par \uc2  President Aleksander Kwasniewski also threw his weight behind the government's bid to weaken the zloty by blaming the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hawkish policy for Poland's export problems in a late television interview by private TVN station. \par \par \uc2  The left-wing government has long complained that interest rates are too high and have caused the worst economic slowdown in a decade and a record 18 percent jobless rate. "The zloty has to be weaker," Belka told the Polish-American Chamber of Commerce in a speech. "I am in favour of opening discussion with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on possible alternatives." \par \par \uc2  Later, Miller said: "The government expects more decisive easing of interest rates and bringing the zloty to a more realistic level, and a more active \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  role." \par \par \uc2  "The overvalued zloty hurts Polish exporters. There should be close cooperation between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government on this issue," he said in a speech on \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid to join the European Union. \par \par \uc2  CENBANK: NO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  The comments, effectively coded calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , were rebuffed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which defended its hands-off approach to Poland's two-year-old free float. \par \par \uc2  "I believe that \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be effective in the current situation," Andrzej Bratkowski, deputy governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told reporters. \par \par \uc2  He added that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would undermine monetary policy and could even hit budget revenues. Analysts say zloty sales would increase the money supply and potentially endanger efforts to fight inflation. \par \par \uc2  Belka, who has in the past surprised markets by calling for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation before Poland adopts the euro later this decade, skirted questions over the precise methods he wants to use to weaken the zloty . \par \par \uc2  "I have already once hinted at possible devaluation. So far, there was no regular discussion on this with the Monetary Policy Council (MPC)," he said. "We should put more emphasis on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  targeting." \par \par \uc2  FOUR-MONTH HIGH \par \par \uc2  The zloty, which reached four-month highs against the dollar on Tuesday and is up 6.6 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and 1.8 percent versus the euro since early February, rose slightly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments in seesaw trade. \par \par \uc2  Bratkowski said the zloty's gains against the dollar reflected the greenback's weakness against the euro - the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Poland's largest export markets. \par \par \uc2  In the neighbouring Czech Republic, like Poland an EU candidate, the government and the national bank joined forces recently to weaken the skyrocketing crown through market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but their move had limited impact. \par \par \uc2  Belka warned the zloty would be under appreciation pressure in coming years if Poland joins the EU in 2004 as planned, which will open the way for adoption of the euro and hence attract foreign capital betting on asset price convergence. \par \par \uc2  He added he was "not against the reversal of the free-float regime," implemented two years ago, which he blamed for artificially bloating the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The free float is the best protection against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis but it also produces an environment in which excessive appreciation is possible," he said, adding however that he was against a fixed exchange rate regime. \par \par \uc2  MONETARY POLICY ROW \par \par \uc2  Belka, normally the "good cop" in a government which has been overwhelmingly critical of the MPC's interest rate policy, also cranked up his rhetoric over the panel's reluctance to cut interest rates faster and to act against the zloty. \par \par \uc2  "I am deeply critical of the the wrong, misdirected policies of the National Bank," he said. \par \par \uc2  Belka said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hampered Poland's drive to catch up with the richer EU by aggressively targetting only one area of economic convergence, namely inflation. \par \par \uc2  Even though the MPC has halved official interest rates since early 2001 to 9.5 percent, they remain six percentage points above inflation, now at a post-communist low of 3.3 