\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED - ANALYSIS-Forint ruled by EU convergence, not politics. \b0\par\par\uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2002\par 17:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      (In the Budapest item "ANALYSIS-Forint ruled by EU \par \par \uc2   convergence, not politics", please read in the 12th paragraph \par \par \uc2   "...attracted subscriptions worth 107 billion forints ($393.7 \par \par \uc2   million)...correcting the dollar figure from $442 million.) \par \par \uc2  A corrected repetition follows. \par \par \uc2  By Sandor Peto \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, April 18 (Reuters) - Hungary's centre-left will struggle to keep a lid on forint gains if it wins a national election run-off on Sunday as euro convergence is giving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a strong boost, analysts said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Socialists, who narrowly beat Prime Minister Viktor Orban's conservative alliance in a first round vote on April 7, have said they would try to take some of the steam out of the forint's recent strength to protect exporters. \par \par \uc2  "The forint's firming trend continues, and it will be even stronger as exports pick up after the recent slowdown," said Istvan Racz, analyst at Credit Suisse First Boston. \par \par \uc2  "The signs of economic pick-up are already here." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said a surge in bond demand and recent forint levels of 242 to the euro indicate optimism over EU convergence is overriding short-term concerns over the election result, inflation and the state budget. \par \par \uc2  "It's clear the markets expect (EU) convergence trends, whoever's in power," said Barbara Nesztor, regional analyst at Commerzbank in Prague. \par \par \uc2  Peter Medgyessy, Socialist candidate for prime minister, told business leaders earlier that a strong forint was diverting firms' resources away from investment in jobs and development. \par \par \uc2  The Socialists are tipped to form a coalition with the liberal Free Democrats and this centre-left grouping favours economic growth at the expense of rushing to cut inflation. \par \par \uc2  The forint has gained 10 percent in nominal terms in the past year and analysts said there would be more speculation on it strengthening further due to convergence with the wealthy euro zone, regardless of which party won. \par \par \uc2  Hungary hopes to join the European Union in 2004 and the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  zone a couple of years later. \par \par \uc2  BOND AUCTION OVER-SUBSCRIBED \par \par \uc2  Huge demand at state bond auctions earlier confounded predictions that a more relaxed centre-left inflation policy would be less favourable for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond markets than a second term for Orban's conservatives, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  An auction of the five-year 2007/D bond - seen as Hungary's convergence benchmark - attracted subscriptions worth 107 billion Hungarian forints ($393.7 million), prompting the government to raise the issue to 40 billion forints from 30 billion. \par \par \uc2  Inflation has dropped to under six percent from nearly 11 percent a year ago, and could dip below five percent by June, although higher world crude oil prices will act against this. \par \par \uc2  Both rival political blocs have pledged voters they will raise wages which, in real net terms, jumped 11.5 percent year-on-year in the first two months of this year. \par \par \uc2  Further wage increases will counter inflation cuts by swelling the budget deficit at a time when purchasing power is surging, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "It seems the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  underestimated the potential for wage growth this year, prompting them to postpone rate cuts in the near future," Lehman Brothers said in a market update. \par \par \uc2  "If the Socialists win, we assume the budget deficit will be revised higher," said Lehman analyst Robert Beange. \par \par \uc2  With little relief from fiscal pressure, Hungary may only be able to keep trimming inflation via exchange rate appreciation, Commerzbank's Nesztor said. \par \par \uc2  "The Socialists would only be able to curb the forint by verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said, noting recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Czech Republic had had only a limited impact. \par \par \uc2  CSFB's Racz said the forint would continue to rise this year, fuelled by growth that is likely to be higher than the recent three percent and continued gains in Hungarian productivity. \par \par \uc2  - For more news, visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.reuters.hu/election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.reuters.hu/election}}}\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020418dy4i00ti6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
