\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Polish budget gap to stay high through 2004-Belka. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Justyna Pawlak \par \uc2 567 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2002\par 20:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Jan 28 (Reuters) - Polish Finance Minister Marek Belka called his 2002 budget plan 'crisis-proof' on Monday, ruling out a revision to increase the deficit later this year, but said the financing gap would not fall in coming years. The three-month-old leftist administration has had to slash spending and shore up revenues to prevent a financial crisis, capping the 2002 budget deficit at 40 billion zlotys ($9.7 billion) or 5.2 percent of gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  Without austerity measures the deficit was set to balloon to 90 billion zlotys or an unfinanceable 11 percent of GDP. \par \par \uc2  "I am not considering the possibility of budget revision this year. This budget is crisis-proof," Belka told Reuters in an interview. \par \par \uc2  Poland's brush with financial collapse stemmed from lavish spending plans of the previous right-wing cabinet, an inefficient public sector and a deep economic slowdown which cut into tax revenues. \par \par \uc2  Economic growth is expected to remain around one percent this year, little changed from last year's growth - the worst in a decade and a major handicap in preparing to join the European Union as soon as 2004. \par \par \uc2  "In March I will know more about what the effect of economic stagnation on revenues. And I will be sure that we assumed really conservative tax inflows," Belka said. \par \par \uc2  But Belka said that reducing the deficit - a key precondition set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for deep interest rate cuts - was not on the card for the next two years. \par \par \uc2  "I am taking it into account that in the next year or two the deficit could oscillate around this year's level or maybe rise slightly to 42 or 43 billion zlotys," he said. \par \par \uc2  ZLOTY \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Belka also said \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's free floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime did not rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the buoyant zloty, which he has tried to talk down for months. \par \par \uc2  "The free float \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime we have does not rule out jaw-boning. I tried that and I tried to charm the zloty to fall to 4.25 to the dollar and it just did not work. The free float does not rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this month, Belka said a 4.25 exchange rate of the zloty to the dollar would be favourable for Polish exporters, but his and other cabinet members' verbal attacks on the zloty attracted little more than shrugs from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The Polish unit rose sharply early this year, reaching 2-1/2-year highs to the dollar as money poured in to take advantage of attractive yields in Polish debt instruments. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland, which shares responsibility for the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, says a free floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not be the subject of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The neighbouring Czech Republic has, however, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cool the crown's strength. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this month, markets speculated that the government may have won \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  backing for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty during a rare face-to-face meeting between ministers and bankers. This sent the zloty tumbling by eight percent. \par \par \uc2  Monetary Policy Council members moved to quell such talk. \par \par \uc2  Asked if he wanted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty, Belka said: "I think we should aim for some depreciation. There are many ways. We can talk, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or cut rates." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020128dy1s011cn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
