\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Zloty edgy pre rate decision, calm elsewhere. \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2001\par 11:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 20 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty traded a touch softer on Friday as players nervously awaited the Monetary Policy Council (MPC) rate decision. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, most emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held to established ranges in the absence of any further ructions in Argentina or Turkey. \par \par \uc2  The zloty handed back some of Thursday's gains, with a few players still jittery about a possible rate cut from the MPC. Most analysts still expect rates to be kept on hold, but weak economic data earlier in the week has cast doubt on the outcome. \par \par \uc2  "The latest data was shocking and clearly shows that something needs to be done," said Marco Annunziata, emerging markets analyst at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  "However, I think the MPC will want to see more evidence that the external environment has settled down before they shift policy," he added. \par \par \uc2  The zloty fell over seven percent against the euro early last week as contagion from Argentina prompted speculators to close out their long positions. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main rate, the minimum 28-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, currently stands at 15.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  At 0900 GMT the zloty traded at 3.6930 to the euro from 3.6726 late on Thursday, and at 4.2250 to the dollar from 4.2195. \par \par \uc2  EXPORTERS BUOY RAND OFF LOWS \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported rand buying from local exporters and from a fund account around the 8.28 level helped the South African unit rally back from early weakness. \par \par \uc2  Ongoing concerns over Argentina continue to make for nervous trade but, with no major developments overnight, players are expecting a quieter session on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Barring fresh shocks from Argentina I think the market could settle down from here heading into the weekend," said one London-based trader. \par \par \uc2  The rand traded at 8.2598 to the dollar from 8.2900 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  LIRA HOLDS FIRM \par \par \uc2  The Turkish lira was in consolidative mood after strong gains in the past two sessions. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment was bolstered by news HSBC had won the tender to buy the troubled Demirbank. Foreign involvement is seen as key to putting the ailing banking sector back on its feet. \par \par \uc2  The lira was quoted at 1,325,000 to the dollar on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokered spot market from 1,340,000 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010720dx7k0079x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
