\par\par \b \uc2  Polish govt think-tank sees rates 600bp too high. \b0\par\par\uc2 148 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2001\par 13:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, May 25 (Reuters) - A Polish government think-tank said on Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current interest rate levels were cramping economic growth and needed to be reduced by 600 basis points. \par \par \uc2  "I repeat, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rates are now 600 basis points too high," RCSS head Jerzy Kropiwnicki told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  "In my view, the MPC should have cut rates by six percentage points in three steps at the start of this year." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main interest rate, the minimum 28-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, is now at 17 percent, following two 100-basis points cuts over the first quarter of this year. \par \par \uc2  Kropiwnicki, who has repeatedly criticised the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's restrictive approach to monetary policy, also said Polish exports would begin to feel the impact of the zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rally from June. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx5p02v97\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
