\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -zloty buoyant, Czech crown and rand soft. \b0\par\par\uc2 634 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 13:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 7 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty remained buoyant on Wednesday, rising to 19-month highs against the dollar and record peaks against the euro, underpinned by an improving economic outlook and new bond issuance. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged off those highs after Polish Finance Minister Jaroslaw Bauc moved to weaken the rally and said the unit could fall in coming months. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown fell to six-week lows against the euro for the second consecutive day and trimmed gains from earlier five-day highs against the dollar. There were lingering fears that crown strength might prompt action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the South African rand continued to struggle, falling to three-week lows against the dollar for the second straight day and nearing four-week lows against the euro. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty is the choice of the day. The zloty opened higher on expectations of strong foreign interest for the 2.5 billion zloty bond tender but has pulled back slightly and we are not yet sure how strong the interest has been," said a trader at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  "We like the zloty because it's a high carry trade opportunity and fundamentals look okay and inflation is dropping. Polish officials are trying to talk it down but we don't expect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  POLISH TENDER EYED \par \par \uc2  The results of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2.5 billion zloty worth of T-bonds were scheduled for later in the day. \par \par \uc2  By 1115 GMT, the zloty rose as far as 3.9470 to the dollar , according to Reuters data. It hit peaks around 3.6835 against the euro . \par \par \uc2  Polish data late Tuesday showed that food prices fell 0.2 percent in the second half of February over the same period in January. The fall in prices fuelled hopes for a sharp decline in February inflation and future rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  A Finance Ministry official said after the data release that CPI probably fell to a year-on-year 6.9-7.0 percent in February from January's 7.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown hit a five-day high of 37.138 per dollar before paring gains. It hit lows around 34.970 per euro . \par \par \uc2  Traders said speculation about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was sparked by the minutes of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's February meeting, released this week. The minutes showed the governing board agreed that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an option the bank "is prepared to use if the need should arise". \par \par \uc2  The Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves edged up marginally to $13.12 billion at the end of February from $13.07 billion in January. \par \par \uc2  RAND SOFT \par \par \uc2  The South African rand fell as far as 7.8913 against the dollar , according to Reuters data, and hit lows around 7.3430 against the euro . \par \par \uc2  Bond exchange data showed that foreigners were net sellers of 66.16 million rand's worth of South African bonds on Tuesday after buying 530.51 million rand on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Tito Mboweni reiterated on Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was targeting inflation and the exchange rate. The market has been wary of the government's decision to introduce an inflation target of between three and six percent, which some feel could further curb current sluggish growth. \par \par \uc2  However, traders expected some supoort from potential capital inflows from an upcoming eurobond issue and Anglo American and De Beers deal. \par \par \uc2  "The bond issuance should be good for the rand, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk is making foreign investors wary," saidStefan Kolek, emerging market strategist at HypoVereinsbank in Munich. \par \par \uc2  "There are still risks that socially and politically things could deteriorate. There are still question marks over whether the government will be able to meet its privatisation target. Mboweni's comments also concerned the market." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3704lvu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
