\par\par \b \uc2  IMF wants transparent Polish govt  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  account. \b0\par\par\uc2 508 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2000\par 17:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, May 18 (Reuters) - The International Monetary Fund said on Thursday \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  should avoid discretionary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and keep the special government \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  account fully transparent to markets. \par \par \uc2  "Discretionary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be avoided," the IMF said in its bi-annual review of Poland's economy. \par \par \uc2  "(But) a case can be made to raise gross reserves according to a predetermined and announced schedule so as to maintain currently strong vulnerability indicators on reserves," it said. \par \par \uc2  Poland's reserves are now at $25.6 billion, more than seven months' worth of imports. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are in the realm of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which fully floated the zloty in April to increase its volatility and thereby discourage short-term foreign portfolio investment. \par \par \uc2  The bank vowed it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market, saying it would go against the idea of the flotation, and is thought to have kept its word during the recent large zloty swings. \par \par \uc2  But the IMF comments seemed to be directed mainly at the finance ministry, which created a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  account in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this year. \par \par \uc2  It can effectively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market by announcing flows in and out of the special foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  account set up to hold revenues from privatisation deals, which used to boost the level of the zloty artificially. \par \par \uc2  But the finance ministry has been vague on how much cash it plans to keep in the account, when it would deposit it there or when it would withdraw it to pay off Poland's external debt. \par \par \uc2  News of such flows can strongly move the shallow local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "The foreign exchage account of the government...should be operated in a manner consistent with the principle of non-discretionary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the IMF wrote. \par \par \uc2  Analysts estimate \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  can expect some $5 billion in foreign inflows in privatisation this year alone. \par \par \uc2  "It will be important therefore that early specific public committments should be made concerning the amount of privatisation receipts that will be deposited into and withdrawn from the government account with the NBP," the IMF said. \par \par \uc2  "Balances in the account should be fully transparent to markets," it added. \par \par \uc2  The IMF also said a government plan to sharply curb the fiscal gap and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aim of improving its inflation targetting framework would create ideal conditions to abolish the remaining controls on short-term capital moves. \par \par \uc2  Poland now allows full zloty convertibility for current account purpuses but has kept some restrictions on short-term portfolio flows to diminish chances of a speculative attack on the zloty. \par \par \uc2  "Given the sizeable spot and forward on-and off-shore market in the zloty, as well as the uninhibited trade in relatively liquid long-term financial instruments it is unlikely that the abolition of the remaining controls would increase Poland's vulnerability," the IMF report said. ((Jan Strupczewski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel.+48 22 653 9700, fax. +48 22 653 9781, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5i008nn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
