\par\par \b \uc2  Polish c.bank gives no pledge on zloty  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2000\par 19:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not pledged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the fully floated zloty if it moves sharply, despite requests for such assurances from some government advisors, a deputy finance minister said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Polish government gave final approval for the full flotation of the zloty\tab   on Tuesday, allowing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to eliminate the unit's 30-point trading band and the 0.3 percent monthly devaluation rate from Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland (NBP) asked for the government's approval in the middle of 1999, prompting some finance ministry advisers to seek assurances the NBP would curb sudden zloty moves, even after the float, to protect exporters. \par \par \uc2  But Deputy Finance Minister Jaroslaw Bauc said no such agreement had not been discussed by the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There was no talks on this issue," Bauc told reporters following a news conference on the flotation. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry advisers had earlier warned steep surges in the zloty, which they said were more likely after the float, could damage Poland's already weak export performance and cause further expansion of the large current account deficit. \par \par \uc2  "We would expect the NBP to declare it would use the flotation carefully and would not allow the current account gap to deteriorate when the zloty appreciates, by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," adviser Witold Orlowski said in January. \par \par \uc2  Poland's current account deficit ran at some eight percent of gross domestic product in February and widened to 7.6 percent of GDP in 1999 from 4.4 percent a year before. \par \par \uc2  A member of the rate-setting Monetary Policy Council, Boguslaw Grabowski, told Tuesday's news conference the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not plan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market but reserved the right to do so if need arose. ((Justyna Pawlak, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, justyna.pawlak@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4b02idp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
