\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Council not planning zloty  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2000\par 18:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Apr 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council is not planning to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the zloty exchange market now the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been fully floated, although it retains the right to do so, a leading Council member said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "We are not planning to participate in the market but we have such a right," said Boguslaw Grabowski at a news conference after the government agreed to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's council request that the zloty should be freed. \par \par \uc2  The government announced on Tuesday it had given the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the zloty market even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would henceforth trade without restrictions. \par \par \uc2  Grabowski also said there were no reasons why the float should affect the zloty's value in the short-term. \par \par \uc2  "I see no economic reasons for the zloty float to influence the market in the short-term," he said. "This will not change the trends on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market." ((Warsaw newsroom +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9781, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4b02ias\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
