\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  would breach float plan - Pruski. \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 14:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, March 22 (Reuters) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market because such a move would contradict plans of floating the zloty, Monetary Policy Council member Jerzy Pruski said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "In mid-1999 we said we wanted to have a floating exchange rate and there is nothing more to add to this statement," Pruski told Reuters in an interview. \par \par \uc2  "Floating is a long-term solution which should not be counterbalanced with short-term consideration and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  The zloty has risen sharply this month, prompting some analysts to consider the possibility of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Pruski rebutted claims by some analysts which suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised rates in Febraury for reasons other than to curb inflation, such as to stun a fast growing current account defcit, which reached 7.6 percent of GDP in 1999. \par \par \uc2  "I believe the problem of the current account deficit is of a structural basis and tools like monetary policy are not very useful in controlling it. Structural changes and a tightening of fiscal policy is mostly needed, not any rate moves," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Monetary Policy Council said it raised interest rates by 100 basis points last month to between 17.5-21.5 percent to help bring inflation down to their end-year target of 5.4-6.8 percent from 10.1 percent in February. ((Wojciech Moskwa, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9781, wojciech.moskwa@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3m03plf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
