\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Zloty, shekel lead Europe higher. \b0\par\par\uc2 780 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2000\par 12:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LONDON, Jan 10 (Reuters) - Hopes that the Polish authorities will agree to a full float of the zloty\tab   lifted the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to four-month highs on Monday in a busy European session for emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par Israel's shekel\tab   rallied as the market welcomed the nomination of a tough \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief, while the Czech crown\tab   gained after robust inflation data reinforced expectations of higher interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The zloty surged to 3.52 percent bid above the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's parity level from 3.0 percent on Friday, buoyed by hopes that the finance minister will agree at a 1500 GMT meeting with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to fully float the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Analysts say such a move would show the authorities were confident in the zloty and would give a psychological boost to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is already allowed to fluctuate in a band of 15 percent on either side of the parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The latest firming of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after a ministry adviser said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should pledge to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account if the floated unit rose sharply. \par \par \uc2  "That seemed to trigger quite a bit of zloty buying," said Bank of America \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Juliet Sampson, adding that she was surprised at the market's reaction. "It looks like there's still going to be a lot of volatility, which has to be taken as a negative." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The zloty\tab      was trading at 4.1538 to the euro compared with 4.1935 on Friday, around levels not seen since late August.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ISRAEL RISKS POLICY CLASH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prime Minister Ehud Barak's choice of David Klein to succeed Jacob Frenkel as Bank of Israel governor, announced on Friday, boosted the shekel on expectations Klein will stick to a tough monetary policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Klein is clearly a hawk, perhaps more hawkish that Frenkel, and that should be taken well by the markets," said Sampson. But the likelihood that Klein would clash more with the finance ministry, which wants lower interest rates, could destabilise economic policy, she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The shekel strengthened to 4.119 to the dollar from 4.1390 on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Czech crown firmed slightly to around three-week highs against the euro after higher-than-expected inflation figures bolstered the view that a long series of interest rate cuts was over.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Consumer prices in December grew 0.5 percent on the month by the headline measure and 0.6 percent at the net level, against market expectations for a 0.3 percent increase on both counts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The crown\tab      was bid at 35.98 to the euro from about 36.00 ahead of the data and 36.02 late on Friday.\par The Slovak crown\tab   was little changed after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap its strength around 42.3 to the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bank has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent the crown from firming around that level level several times in December and again in January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The crown\tab      was recently trading at 42.262 against the euro from around 42.259 on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par including the change versus late New York trade the previous day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the change in the year to date.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , formerly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reflect new market norms. All other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are quoted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise or fall of the dollar or euro value.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   CLOSE\par Czech Rep.\tab \tab    36.00   36.02   -0.06%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab  4.16    4.19    -0.82%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 254.64  254.43  0.08%\par Slovakia\tab \tab      42.26   42.26   0.01%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab 18,315  18,307  0.04%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab 5.50    5.37    2.42%\par South Africa\tab \tab  6.07    6.05    0.28%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab   72.45   72.60   -0.21%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab  4.115   4.142   -0.65%\par Turkey\tab \tab \tab  540,200 538,880 0.24%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \