\par\par \b \uc2  Poland finmin wants cbank to cap zloty after float. \b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2000\par 15:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Jan 9 (Reuters) - The Polish finance ministry should seek assurances from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty if the unit rose steeply, before agreeing to fully float the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a ministry advisor said on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  A substantial zloty appreciation would hurt Poland's exports and harm the already-strained current account deficit, Witold Orlowski told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Leszek Balcerowicz is due to meet members of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision-making Monetary Policy Council (RPP) at 1500 GMT on Monday to discuss the zloty's full flotation. \par \par \uc2  "We would expect the National Bank of Poland to declare it would use the flotation carefully and would not allow the current account gap to deteriorate when the zloty appreciates, by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Orlowski said. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account is still at risk and I can see a scenario when the zloty appreciates greatly this year due to privatisation inflows...That would harm the current account and Poland cannot afford to allow that," he said. \par \par \uc2  Poland's current account deficit is expected to have widened to some seven percent of the GDP in 1999 from 4.3 percent in the previous year following a sharp decrease in exports. It is seen stabilising around seven percent in 2000. \par \par \uc2  The 10-member RPP, which alone sets Poland's monetary policy and co-decides with the government on changes in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, asked the government to make a decision on freeing the zloty last year. \par \par \uc2  But the government has been delaying the move, fearing that the zloty would become prone to destabilising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation. \par \par \uc2  The zloty jumped last week following reports of the finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting, on expectations that the long-awaited float was nearing, reaching four-month highs around three percent above parity on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But ministry and bank officials have said the Monday meeting would not necessarily be conclusive. \par \par \uc2  The zloty now trades inside a 30 percent daily band, centred on the so-called parity rate set daily by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a basket of the dollar and the euro. \par \par \uc2  The parity is adjusted by a devaluation factor of 0.3 percent per month to compensate for Poland's inflation. \par \par \uc2  The free flotation of the Polish unit would mean scrapping the daily trading band, the crawling devaluation and the parity rate. The move would give the zloty a boost, analysts say. ((Justyna Pawlak, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax. +48 22 653 9781, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1905k6o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
