\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW-Polish c.bank determined to defend zloty. \b0\par\par\uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 1999\par 12:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HELSINKI, Nov 12 (Reuters) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  will spare no expense \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the zloty if such a need arises, deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Ryszard Kokoszczynski said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "We are always ready to defend the zloty. We have in the past \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a number of times for various reasons. We have set procedures and are closely observing the market," Kokoszczynski told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "To make such a decision is a question of seconds rather than minutes," he said in an interview during a two-day summit of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with eastern European central bankers. \par \par \uc2  Asked how much of its roughly $26 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be willing to spend on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Kokoszczysnki said: "As much as it takes." \par \par \uc2  A week ago the zloty tumbled to all-time lows on a deteriorating macroeconomic picture and worries that the respected Finance Minister Leszek Balcerowicz would resign, but it rebounded as political tensions eased. The NBP did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Early on Friday the zloty traded around 4.3 percent below the centre of its daily trading range against last week's lows at 5.6 percent below parity. \par \par \uc2  Kokoszczynski said he was not worried by a possible withdrawal of foreign portfolio capital from Poland, because foreign holdings are relatively small compared to state reserves and because the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is volatile. \par \par \uc2  "If somebody wants to sell zlotys at all costs, even paying a 10 or 15 percent premium for withdrawing, then he must be expecting a catastrophe and there are no fundamental reasons to expect such a black scenario," he said. Sentiment on the zloty has soured since inflation began to increase in mid-1999 and it became apparent exports were not recovering from last year's Russian crisis. \par \par \uc2  The current account gap has grown to an estimated seven percent of gross domestic product this year, from 1998's 4.3 percent of GDP. \par \par \uc2  Kokoszczynski said there was no single current account deficit level which would be dangerous for the Polish economy. \par \par \uc2  As the deficit was caused by investment and not consumption imports and was financed by long-term investment, numbers should not be a "fetish" for analysts, he said. ((Wojciech Moskwa, warsaw newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9781, wojciech.moskwa@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvbc0034s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
