\par\par \b \uc2  Polish c.bank sees no need to support zloty now. \b0\par\par\uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 1999\par 08:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Nov 4 (Reuters) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not currently see a need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the falling zloty, deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Ryszard Kokoszczynski told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The zloty tumbled to all-time lows on Thursday after Finance Minister Leszek Balcerowicz threatened he would quit if parliament failed to pass his tax-cutting reform in time for it to be implemented next year. \par \par \uc2  "For the time being the situation on the market would not justify \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially since the developments of the last two days are of a political nature," Kokoszczynski said. \par \par \uc2  He said the bank would consider \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the zloty weakening lasted long enough to threaten its medium-term inflation target, which envisages bringing price growth below four percent in 2003 from 8-9 percent in 1999. \par \par \uc2  "If the weakness does not stem from fundamentals and lasts too long from the point of view of our medium-term goals and if we decide that direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are better than using other monetary policy instruments, then we will do it," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to bring inflation down to 5.4-6.8 percent in December 2000 and has already raised its main \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by 100 bp in September to defend that goal from a recent inflation surge. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect the bank to raise its interest rates again on November 17 in response to fast growing production which is not accompanied by exports growth, suggesting high domestic demand and inflationary pressure. \par \par \uc2  Kokoszczynski said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be all the more questionable because of the volatility of a market that has been thinned by the departure of foreign investors wary of millennium computer bug risks. \par \par \uc2  "The market is extremely thin and fundamentals have little influence on what is happening and it will probably stay that way until the end of the year," he said. \par \par \uc2  The zloty plummeted to 4.86 percent weaker than the parity rate on Thursday morning on the Balcerowicz resignation worries, but rebounded to around 4.2 later in the day on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments there were no fundamental reasons for such weakening. \par \par \uc2  Kokoszczynski also said that the macroeconomic data still to hit the market in the next two months would more likely be positive than negative. \par \par \uc2  "The poor data has already been priced in, so unless there is more bad news from politics, what we can expect is data which would improve the perception of the economy," Kokoszczynski said. \par \par \uc2  He said the market already knew that year-on-year inflation would be somewhere between eight and nine percent in December against 8.6 percent in December 1998. \par \par \uc2  He also said the current account deficit would most probably be smaller than the 7.5 percent of GDP predicted by a government think-tank, giving a the market a positive impulse. ((Jan Strupczewski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel.+48 22 653 9700, fax. +48 22 653 9781, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvb500iyf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
