\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging market  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Zloty at fresh lows, rand firms. \b0\par\par\uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 1999\par 10:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 5 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty tumbled to fresh record lows on Friday as the finance minister's threat to resign continued to undermine the market, while the South African rand strengthened on strong foreign demand for bonds, emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialists said. \par \par \uc2  The zloty opened more than 5.2 percent below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's parity rate, a percentage point lower than Thursday's close, as it continued to reel from poor economic data and Finance Minister Leszek Balcerowicz's ultimatum to resign if parliament did not pass his tax reform plan. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded strongly, moving back above the five percent level, amid speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The deputy governor of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Ryszard Kokoszczynski, told Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not justified "for the time being" but that it would consider stepping in if the weakening lasted long enough to threaten its inflation target. \par \par \uc2  "If the price action just became one way they will step in as they stepped in on the other side," when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was strong, said Jake Moore, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Barclays Capital. \par \par \uc2  He said the zloty might be further hurt by news on Thursday that U.S.-based telecoms firm SBC Communications had withdrawn its bid for 25-35 percent of Polish state-controlled telephone operator TPSA. \par \par \uc2  The move means France Telecom , now the lone bidder, may reduce its offer price and decrease the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  privatisation receipts the government plans to exchange in the market. \par \par \uc2  At 0907 GMT the zloty was trading at 4.5153 bid to the euro, stronger than an early low of 4.5490 but weaker than 4.5050 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  CZECH CROWN GAINS \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in Europe, the Czech crown gained against the euro as the euro remained weak against the dollar in the wake of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate rise. The crown was trading at 36.606 to the euro versus 36.690 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian forint held steady at the strong end of its trading band even after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would cut its base rate to 15 percent from 15.5. The cut followed a 25 basis point reduction in benchmark rates on Thursday. The forint was at 254.97 against the euro versus 255.05. \par \par \uc2  The rand strengthened for a second day on the back of firmer South African bonds, climbing to 6.109 to the dollar from 6.1270 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Benchmark bond yields fell below 14 percent, a level they have not closed below since June 1998, on the eve of last year's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  Bonds are benefiting from stability in global debt markets and comments from Deputy Reserve Bank Governor Gill Marcus that the bank was using an informal three to five percent inflation target, Moore said. \par \par \uc2  "The market's getting to grips with the Reserve Bank being committed to reducing inflation expectations," he said. \par \par \uc2  In Asia, the Indonesian rupiah dipped to 6,795 to the dollar from 6,740 and the Korean won slipped to 1,186 from 1,184. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab   LATEST  PVS CLS  PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ON YEAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab     36.61   36.71   -0.27%  5.20%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab   4.53    4.50    0.72%   11.24%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab  254.86  254.79  0.03%   1.46%\par Slovakia\tab \tab \tab 43.54   43.54   0.00%   1.26%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab  17,085  17,090  -0.03%  56.03%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab  4.80    4.80    0.00%   22.14%\par South Africa\tab \tab   6.11    6.12    -0.24%  4.48%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab    74.65   74.55   0.13%   21.19%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab   4.218   4.235   -0.40%  2.40%\par Turkey\tab \tab \tab   489,140 488,180 0.20%   54.91%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LATAM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexico\tab \tab \tab   9.46    9.47    -0.13%  -3.86%\par Brazil\tab \tab \tab   1.9190  1.9190  0.00%   58.98%\par Venezuela\tab \tab      631.25  631.25  0.00%   11.82%\par Chile\tab \tab \tab    549.40  549.40  0.00%   16.84%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ASIA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore\tab \tab      1.668   1.665   0.20%   0.72%\par Hong Kong\tab \tab      7.771   7.771   0.01%   0.32%\par China\tab \tab \tab    8.278   8.278   0.00%   -0.02%\par Indonesia\tab \tab      6,800   6,750   0.74%   -14.47%\par Thailand\tab \tab \tab 38.57   38.35   0.57%   6.84%\par Philippines\tab \tab    40.02   40.00   0.05%   4.35%\par Taiwan\tab \tab \tab   31.71   31.60   0.33%   -1.23%\par South Korea\tab \tab    1,186   1,184   0.17%   0.08%\par India\tab \tab \tab    43.41   43.30   0.26%   2.17%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvb500gro\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
