\par\par \b \uc2  Poland c.banker says does not target zloty level. \b0\par\par\uc2 134 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 1999\par 11:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SALZBURG, Austria July 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to influence the level of the zloty, governor Hanna Gronkiewicz-Waltz told Reuters in an interview on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said Monday's action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "more correctly arbitrage than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  On Monday and last Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  undertook its first \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 10 months, buying and selling euros for zlotys to smooth the market. \par \par \uc2  Gronkiewicz-Waltz told Reuters that the zloty's full float could happen within 12 months after discussions with the government. \par \par \uc2  She added that Poland could not expect any downward move on interest rates in the near future. \par \par \uc2  ((-David Chance, Salzburg newsroom, 07990 560431)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7105dyg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
