\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's monetary council unlikely to cut rates on Wed. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Justyna Pawlak \par \uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 1999\par 13:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 13 (Reuters) - Analysts expect Poland's Monetary Policy Council (RPP) to hold interest rates steady at its meeting on Wednesday, because inflation may rise later this year after a sharp fall in recent months. \par \par \uc2  Analysts from Polish and foreign banks said a rate cut was unlikely even after the Hungarian and Czech monetary authorities cut their interest rates following the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (ECB) rate 0.5 point rate lowering last week. \par \par \uc2  "It's a tough call after the ECB decision and if anythinig the move would be small, but I don't think they will cut at all," said Thomas Brown, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan in London. \par \par \uc2  "The CPI is a key driver. If we have an uptick in inflation for the first time in 12 months, which would be in line with the finance ministry's forecasts, then that would suggest inflationary pressures," he said. The finance ministry estimated prices rose 1.1 percent in March against 0.6 percent in February, bringing the year-on-year index up to 6.2 percent from 5.6 percent in February. Official inflation data for March will be published by the Central Statistical Office on April 15. \par \par \uc2  "They (the RPP) are afraid of the perception that a rate cut would provide an inflationary impulse and that such expectations would actually boost inflation," said Sonja Gibbs, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Nomura International in London. \par \par \uc2  The International Monetary Fund recently said that Poland should be cautious about further cuts after January's sweeping 250-300 basis point rate cut and should wait to see its effects on the economy before easing policy again. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main market rate, the minimum 28-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, is now at 13.0 percent, the discount rate is at 15.5 percent and the lombard rate at 17.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that both external and internal inflationary pressures have increased recently, and the RPP may have to be more cautious with monetary policy after it lowered its 1999 inflation target to 6.6-7.8 percent at the March 24 meeting. "It is possible that inflation will rise from now until the end of the year. After the RPP lowered its inflationary target, they cannot allow themselves to cut rates now," said Mateusz Szczurek, economist at ING Barings in Warsaw. "Strong dollar, weak zloty, the rebound in oil prices and the recently imposed food tariffs are likely to boost inflation," he said. \par \par \uc2  But analysts also expect the RPP may still lower interest rates by some 100-250 basis points by year-end. \par \par \uc2  "If economic growth doesn't show signs of improvement, the zloty stays on the strong side of parity and the April budget comes out well, maybe they will cut rates even in mid-May," Nomura's Gibbs said. \par \par \uc2  Poland's gross domestic product growth slowed to 4.8 percent in 1998 from 6.8 percent in 1997 after the Russian crisis and slower growth in Western Europe depressed exports. In 1999, GDP is expected to grow by some four to 4.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  "They will want to cut before they free-float the zloty, which they indicated they would do, because liberalising the exchange rate policy without cutting rates would be a recipe for appreciation," JP Morgan's Brown said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts do not expect the RPP to change the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy at the Wednesday meeting. ((Warsaw newsroom, tel +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9781, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv4d02zvq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
