\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Zloty Lower On Continued Selling After Rate Cuts \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1999\par 10:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty (PLZ) is lower against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket midmorning Friday, as investors continue to sell the zloty after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp rate cuts Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also said falls on global stock markets are causing the zloty to weaken. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty is 5.2% above the mid-point against its basket, down from around 5.75% at the close of trading Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a dollar/euro basket and is devalued at a rate of 0.5% a month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 12.5% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday cut the 28-day money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to 13% from 15.5%, the Lombard rate to 17% from 20% and the discount rate to 15.5% from 18.25%. Market participants had expected a rate cut of between 100 and 150 basis points. \par \par \uc2  "It's a consequence of the rate cuts," said Tomasz Wlad, broker at AmerBrokers. Wlad said interest in Polish debt is declining and investors are closing positions because the rate cut has made Polish debt less attractive. \par \par \uc2  Around 0910 GMT, the dollar was at PLZ3.5900, up from PLZ3.5700 at the opening and up from Thursday's fixing of PLZ3.5730. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at PLZ4.1680, up from Thursday's fixing of PLZ4.1330. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at PLZ3.7868 and for the euro at PLZ4.3946. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is 5.2% below its parity rate, and the euro is 5.2% below parity. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates are between 14.00% and 15.20%. \par \par \uc2  -By Jennifer Laidlaw; 48-22 622-2766; jlaidlaw@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0937GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1m00l2o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
