\par\par \b \uc2  Polish rate cut seen in December, maybe Wednesday. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wojcieh Moskwa \par \uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 1998\par 17:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Dec 8 (Reuters) - Poland's Monetary Council (RPP) is expected to trim interest rates by at least 100 bp in December, but analysts are divided whether the policy making body will make its move as soon as this Wednesday, when it meets. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said on Tuesday that falling inflation and slower economic growth pointed toward an interest rate cut in the near-term, but some expected the 10-member council to hold off decisions until its next meeting on December 16. \par \par \uc2  "I expect a 100 basis point cut in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate on Wednesday and no changes in official rates," said Krzysztof Rybinski, chief economist at ING Barings in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  The 28-day money-market drainage rate, called the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, is now set at a minimum of 17 percent. \par \par \uc2  Official rates, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said reflected longer-term policy trends, now stand at 22 percent for the lombard and 20 percent for the discount rate. \par \par \uc2  Other analysts expected more drastic rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  "The likelihood is greater that they will move on the 16th rather than tomorrow and my forecast is for about a 200 basis point cut," said Juliet Sampson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of America in London. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll released on Tuesday showed 20 of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 21 largest banks expected a cut in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate and 13 banks saw a cut in the lombard rate this month. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said financial markets have mostly priced in the widely-expected loosening, with the zloty slipping in recent days while stocks regained ground lost in November. \par \par \uc2  "About 100 basis points have been priced in already and if there is a 200 bp cut then we could see the zloty slip a touch," Bank of America's Sampson said. She added her year-end target for the zloty was 3.55 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the zloty was at 3.5095 to the dollar and at 2.0995 to the mark, or 6.19 percent above its trading band mid-point. The zloty can fluctuate in a band of 12.5 percent on either side of its parity rate centre. \par \par \uc2  Warsaw shares eased 0.4 percent to 12,227 points on Tuesday but remain six percent higher than at the start of December. Analysts said the Tuesday easing was due to profit taking after sharp gains in anticipation of the rate cut. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said interest rate cuts must accompany falls in inflation to keep Poland's economic engine, hurt by the collapse of Russia and slowing growth in the EU, in high gear. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Leszek Balcerowicz expects the economy to grow five percent in 1999, but most analysts are not as upbeat. \par \par \uc2  "The slowing of economic growth can be quite extensive next year, especially over the first two quarters. Overall GDP should grow 4.5 percent against 5.5 percent in 1998," said Krzysztof Bledowski, chief economist at WoodCommerz in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duc8030ec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
