\par\par \b \uc2  Early zloty sets new 12-wk high amid upbeat mood. \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1998\par 10:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Nov 10 (Reuters) - The buoyant zloty hit a new three-month high early on Tuesday, breaching a psychological level of 8.0 percent above the parity rate amid improving investment prospects in emerging markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0940 GMT the zloty firmed to 8.11/8.07 percent above the parity rate against the opening 8.09/7.98 percent and Monday's 8.01 percent fix. \par \par \uc2  It traded at 3.4380/95 to the dollar against 3.4360/00 at the start and at 2.0350/60 to the mark agianst 2.0370/00. \par \par \uc2  The zloty last traded above 8.0 percent stronger than parity in mid-August before its was engulfed by Russia's economic and political crisis, during which it plunged below its trading band mid-point. \par \par \uc2  "Improved sentiment on emerging markets seems the main factor behind the zloty's rise. It was partly due to foreign buying, although foreign traders are less active today," said Piotr Lancucki, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at BNP-Dresdner in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that recent gains on many markets and an expected mulit-billion dollar bail-out aid package for Brasil has lifted hopes for economic stability in emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  One-year Non-Delivery Forwards (NDFs) dipped to 14.2/14.7 on Tuesday against Monday's 14.5/15.1 percent, signalling some foreign entry into zloty instruments, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market did not expect the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) to step in with dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the time being to curb the zloty's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  "Very probably the NBP will stay away from the market until the zloty approaches 10 percent. The band was widened so they have no need to defend it at the moment," a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2  In late October the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council widened the zloty's band to plus/minus 12.5 percent on either side of a parity rate from the previous plus/minus 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  The zloty's parity rate is now gradually devalued at a pace of 0.5 percent per month to neutralise Poland's high inflation. ((Pawel Kozlowski, Warsaw Newsroom, tel. +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780, warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duba04sdb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
