\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Zloty -2: Sale Of BPH Stake Strengthening Zloty \b0\par\par\uc2 238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 1998\par 10:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers also said speculation that Germany's Bayerische Hypo- und\par Vereinsbank AG is buying zlotys to pay for its stake in Bank\par Przemyslowo-Handlowy SA is another reason for the zloty's sharp climb\par over the last few days.\par    Recently, HypoVereinsbank bought a 37% stake in BPH for DEM1\par billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "That's been having a lot of impact on the zloty's strength over the\par last few days," said Piotr Konarski, dealer at Westdeutsche Landesbank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign investors have returned to the Polish market on calmer world financial markets, a move which is helping the zloty to strengthen. \par \par \uc2  Konarski said if the zloty continues to strengthen so rapidly, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the parity rate for the dollar at PLZ3.7015 and for the mark at PLZ2.2330. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is 7.6% below its parity rate, and the mark is 7.6% below parity. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 0.5% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 12.5% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates are between 17.00% and 17.50%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Jennifer Laidlaw; 48-22 622-2766; jlaidlaw@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-11-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0946GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 