\par\par \b \uc2  Wrap/Polish Zloty -2: Supportive Words From  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1998\par 19:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Although \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  opted not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to support the zloty Friday, several officials made statements intended to soothe investors and to lend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  some verbal support. \par \par \uc2  "There is no reason to worry," said Dariusz Rosati, a member of the Monetary Policy Council. "These type of big swings that we've seen in the last two days aren't something pleasant, but they don't worry me because they aren't a symptom of any serious disease on our side." \par \par \uc2  With the zloty hovering around its parity rates against the dollar and Deutsche mark, Rosati said there was no reason for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may move to "smooth" market volatility if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Because Russia accounts for less than 10% of Polish trade volume, the Polish economy won't suffer from the devaluation of the ruble, said Deputy Finance Minister Jaroslaw Bauc. \par \par \uc2  "If the crisis continues in Russia, there will be some effects on the real sphere in Poland, but I wouldn't panic," Bauc said. He said the prospect of rising interest rates and an economic slowdown in Western Europe posed a greater threat. \par \par \uc2  Already, some adventurous investors are starting to cautiously build up zloty positions, taking advantage of what they see as temporary weakness, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty already offers tremendous value," said Mateusz Szczurek, an economist at ING Barings. \par \par \uc2  David Simmonds, head of research for central and Eastern Europe at Citibank in London, predicted the zloty would trade in a wide range of plus-or-minus 3.0% around the midpoint of its band in the next few weeks. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 21-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1702GMT \par \par \uc2  1193 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8l0752t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
