\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty rides to new record high, nears top of band. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wojciech Moskwa \par \uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 1998\par 17:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Aug 4 (Reuters) - The zloty ripped through strong resistance at nine percent above parity on Tuesday to close at a new record high as more foreign money poured into Poland. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 9.08/9.03 percent above the parity rate, bettering Monday's record close of 8.89/8.84 percent and nearing the top of its daily fluctuation band of plus/minus 10 percent on either side of the parity rate centre. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local market for the second day running on Tuesday, after buying some $200 million last week to cool the zloty. This gave the Polish unit time to gather upward momentum, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty is hot. We should see more gains tomorrow and without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market could even test the 10 percent trading band limit," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a foreign bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Other players said the zloty could slip from record highs amid light profit-taking after going so far in past weeks. \par \par \uc2  "We will probably see some profit-taking soon...but unless something fundamental changes in Poland, you can see the zloty trading well above eight percent," said Ryszard Bublik, trader at Nomura International in London. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 3.4320/40 per dollar, against 3.4390/05 on Monday, and at 1.9246/56 to the mark, against 1.9255/65. \par \par \uc2  Foreigners were interested in zloty debt because the country's rates were still high in real terms, making it a good convergence play as Poland seeks EU accession, and because further rate cuts were expected still in 1998, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be able to continue to carry out costly \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the longer term, so a pre-emptive rate cut could be in the works, they added. \par \par \uc2  "It will be very interesting to see how the (decision-making) RPP monetary policy council reacts to the zloty's rise when it meets on August 19," Nomura's Bublik said. \par \par \uc2  The zloty's trading band centre - the parity rate - is set each day by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  according to the value of a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a devaluation factor. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's parity depreciates by 0.65 percent per month against a basket to help keep Poland's exports competitive in a context of double-digit domestic inflation. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's 700 million zloty fixed rate T-bond tender should receive a warm welcome from paper-hungry foreign investors despite an expected fall of several percentage points in yields, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The secondary market is depleted and clients want size, meaning they will want to buy at the tender," said Wlodzimierz Kado, dealer at Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  The yield of the 13-percent two-year bond, due October 12, 2000, was seen falling to around 14.1-13.9 percent against an average yield of 18.49 at the previous tender in early July. \par \par \uc2  The 12-percent. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du840178j\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs